<title>GERMANY: Germans seek barley, rye exports from intervention.</title>
<headline>Germans seek barley, rye exports from intervention.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders applied for the export of 50,000 tonnes of barley and 4,000 tonnes of rye from intervention stores to third countries, intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bids were made under the last weekly EU export tender in 1996.</p>
<p>The next tender will be held on Jan 9.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
